  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "What is stored where",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "\nThis platform's data lives in **two very different places**, and both are on\nthis page.\n\n**PostgreSQL** holds application state \u2014 conversations, messages, cross-chat\nmemory, the web-search memory (`web_pages`, `web_searches`, `web_results`),\ncrawl records and Deep Research runs. It has a real exporter, so everything\nbelow is live server statistics.\n\n**Files on the `data` volume** hold everything else, and none of them speak a\nwire protocol: the Salesforce warehouse is a **DuckDB** file, the two vector\nindexes are **LanceDB** directories, and the sync worker lands **Parquet**.\nThose are measured by walking the volume read-only \u2014 size, file count, and how\nlong ago anything was written.\n\nThe number to watch is **warehouse snapshot age**. The sync worker publishes an\natomic read copy each cycle; if that age keeps climbing, every Salesforce\nanswer is quietly being served from a stale copy while every container still\nreports healthy.\n"
      }
    },
